#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:1
msgid "Variables and Assignments"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:3
msgid ""
"Module-level variables may be created by assigning them a value with `:=`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:5
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"foo := \"hello\"\n"
"bar := \"world\"\n"
"\n"
"baz:\n"
"  echo {{ foo + \" \" + bar }}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:13
msgid "All variables in a module may be printed:"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:15
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just --evaluate\n"
"bar := \"world\"\n"
"foo := \"hello\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:21
msgid "Or the value of a single variable:"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:28
msgid ""
"All variables in a submodule or a single variable in a submodule may be "
"printed with a path to the submodule or variable<sup>1.49.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:31
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just --evaluate bob::bar\n"
"x := \"world\"\n"
"y := \"hello\"\n"
"$ just --evaluate bob::bar::y\n"
"hello\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:39
msgid ""
"The format of exported variables may be controlled with `--evaluate-"
"format`<sup>1.49.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:42
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just --evaluate --evaluate-format shell\n"
"bar=\"world\"\n"
"foo=\"hello\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:48
msgid "The default format is `--evaluate-format just`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/variables-and-assignments.md:50
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just --evaluate --evaluate-format just\n"
"bar := \"world\"\n"
"foo := \"hello\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
